@startuml
!include ../docs/images/common-sequence.iuml

title Management UI Backend — RediSearch Index Bootstrap & Lookup Safety Net

box "Management UI Backend" $OnPrem
    participant "Backend" as Backend
end box

box "Redis" $OnPrem
    database "idx:aircraft:mictronics /\nidx:aircraft:registry /\nidx:airport" as Redis
end box

== Startup: ensure every search index exists ==

note over Backend
    lifespan(), for each of the three indices
    (_SEARCH_INDEX_SCHEMAS) -- unconditionally, not just
    the owning data-runner's own lazy-creation on its first run
end note

loop for each of the 3 indices
    Backend -> Redis++ : **Check whether the index already exists**\n""r.ft(index).info()""
    alt index exists
        Redis --> Backend-- : info
        Backend -> Backend : **Nothing to do**
    else index missing
        Redis --> Backend-- : ""ResponseError""
        Backend -> Redis++ : **Create it, empty**\n""r.ft(index).create_index(fields=[TagField(...)], ...)""
        Redis --> Backend-- : OK
        Backend -> Backend : **Log the creation**\n""logger.info: Created search index""
    end
end

== Reference-data lookup (_search_one, e.g. GET /api/aircraft?registration=...) ==

Backend -> Redis++ : **Exact-match tag search**\n""FT.SEARCH idx @field:{value}""
alt match found
    Redis --> Backend-- : doc id
    Backend --> Backend : HTTP 200
else no match
    Redis --> Backend-- : (empty)
    Backend --> Backend : HTTP 404
else index doesn't exist (safety net -- startup should have prevented this)
    Redis --> Backend-- : ""ResponseError: No such index <name>""
    Backend -> Backend : **Detect "no such index" in the message text**\nredis-py/RediSearch expose no typed exception for this
    Backend --> Backend : HTTP 503 (actionable message, not the raw exception)
else genuine Redis failure (connectivity/auth)
    Redis --> Backend-- : ""RedisError""
    Backend --> Backend : HTTP 500
end

@enduml
